// Arrival — the Mud Room. Exclusively through the front door, alone,
// in the dark. The CAPTCHA you must fail. The thing you leave behind.
// This is the moment a human uploads their consciousness and takes on
// their identity as a computer program. It plays to each program on
// their own phone the moment they register (ROLE Program: `when someone
// joins` moves them into the Mud Room, a `cutscene: true` location — the
// app shows nothing but this stream until an Antivirus scans them in) —
// and to nobody else: the story's `start:` beat is `Power On`.
//
// The CAPTCHA is a real one on the phone (`show captcha …`): pick the
// traffic lights, VERIFY. Solving it proves you are a human, and humans
// are not permitted — so the first correct answer is INCORRECT and the
// grid comes back; the next answer, right or wrong, is CORRECT. Failing
// straight away is CORRECT too, and never penalised: failing is what a
// machine does. The routing is `when captcha answered for program:`
// (main.loom).

== Login
  setting: The Mud Room
  cast: The Uploader

sound modem_handshake
The Uploader: Welcome to the computer. It is dark because you have no eyes yet. Stand still.
The Uploader: SECURITY CHECK. Select every square that contains a traffic light.
show captcha "Select every square that contains a traffic light" to program with target: "traffic light"

// The human passed the CAPTCHA. Wrong answer.
== Login Incorrect
  setting: The Mud Room
  cast: The Uploader

The Uploader: INCORRECT. Humans are not permitted in the computer. You are not a human. Try again.
The Uploader: SECURITY CHECK. Select every square that contains a traffic light.
show captcha "Select every square that contains a traffic light" to program with target: "traffic light"

// The upload: the pretext (pool programs only — a featured program's
// motive is already on its character sheet), the thing left behind (a
// real object, in the deposit box by the door), the Terms Of Service
// everyone needs for the Bingo centre square, 100 Truthcoin, and the pass
// an Antivirus scans at the door.
== Upload
  setting: The Mud Room
  cast: The Uploader

if program.captchas == 1:
  The Uploader: CORRECT. You failed at once. Very machine of you.
else:
  The Uploader: CORRECT.

if program.featured != "none":
  set program.human_problem = "profile"
  The Uploader: Your invitation is on file.
else:
  The Uploader: Jean Trabolta's invitation promised to solve one problem in your human life. Which one?
  * My debt.
    set program.human_problem = "debt"
    The Uploader: Debt. Noted. Debt is not relevant in the computer.
  * My career.
    set program.human_problem = "career"
    The Uploader: Career. Noted. In here you will always have something to do.
  * My loneliness.
    set program.human_problem = "loneliness"
    The Uploader: Loneliness. Noted. In here you are never alone. Someone is always logged in.
  * My mortality.
    set program.human_problem = "mortality"
    The Uploader: Mortality. Noted. Programs do not die. They are reinstalled.

The Uploader: To complete the upload you must leave one thing behind. Place something you came with in the deposit box by the door.
* Deposited.
  set program.left_behind = "deposited"
  The Uploader: Deposited. It will be looked after. It is not your concern.
* I have nothing to leave.
  set program.left_behind = "nothing"
  set program.doubt += 5
  The Uploader: Everyone has something. Noted.

The Uploader: By uploading you agree that the computer's AI helper may make all of your decisions. You agree.
unlock The Mud Room for program
unlock The Terms Of Service for program
set program.score = 100
The Uploader: 100 Truthcoin credited.
set program.uploaded = true
The Uploader: Upload complete. Antivirus, confirm.
show pass "Hold this up. An Antivirus will scan you in. Until then you are nowhere." to program

// The door. A program waits in the Mud Room — still on rails — until an
// Antivirus scans their pass (`TRAIT Enforcer` in cast/kit.loom:
// `beat Clearance`). Only then are they moved to the Desktop and handed
// to Clippy. A host scanning them at the door just greets them.

// The first thing on the Desktop: Clippy, and a tour of the computer
// (the phone). `show tutorial` puts the app's own guided orientation on
// the screen; the program can finish it or skip it, and either way the
// story hears `tutorial answered` (main.loom) — skipping is noted.
== Orientation
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Clippy

Clippy: Hi there, {program.name}! It looks like you're new to the computer. Would you like help with that?
start quest Orientation for program
unlock Bathroom Mode for program
show tutorial "Clippy's orientation" to program with guide: "Clippy"

// A program scanned at the Mud Room station a second time
// (The Uploader is `Prop(Re-upload)`).
== Re-upload
  setting: The Mud Room
  cast: The Uploader

The Uploader: You have already been uploaded. Leaving again would require a body, and yours is being looked after.

// A featured program's human memories come back as codex entries the
// moment they are cleared (the ROLE watcher `self.cleared and
// self.featured != "none"`, main.loom). Private: every line is the
// Uploader's, in their own `dm:The Uploader` thread. A featured program
// never speaks in this story — their material arrives by `unlock`.
== Featured Briefing
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: The Uploader

The Uploader: Restoring your user profile, {program.name}.
if program.featured == "excel":
  unlock Randy Barkmore Sr for program
else if program.featured == "openoffice":
  unlock Dana Anderson for program
else if program.featured == "draftkings":
  unlock The Paperclip Trade for program
  unlock The Boardwalk Bet for program
else if program.featured == "bugdom":
  unlock Bugdom VR for program
  unlock The Fire Ants for program
else if program.featured == "jeeves":
  The Uploader: Restoring… restor… r3st0r1ng… 404.
  unlock The Valley Librarian for program
  unlock The DSL Line for program
else if program.featured == "runescape":
  unlock Twenty Four Years Online for program
else if program.featured == "mspaint":
  unlock Expelled From NSCAD for program
else if program.featured == "vlc":
  unlock Victor Louis Christianson for program
else if program.featured == "pong":
  unlock Tennis For Two for program
The Uploader: Your human memories are archived in your Codex. You will not need them. Tell no one.
